{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Indeed, with you the wisdom will die</b> — With you, on account of your folly, as in: their wisdom is rotten [n]."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the phrase אמנם כי אתם עם תמות החכמה, which reflects the verse's wording but with עם (\"with\") in place of the standard עמכם; retained as he quotes it. The allusion is to Isaiah 19:11, נסרחה חכמתם. This comment stands alone with no surrounding context in the source provided."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:25.692890941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}